# agmsg for Cursor CLI

Use agmsg only through scripts under `~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/`.
Do not directly read or edit the agmsg DB, config files, or team data.

Start by identifying this Cursor project:

```bash
~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/whoami.sh "$(pwd)" cursor
```

If not joined, ask for team and agent name, then run:

```bash
~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/join.sh <team> <agent_name> cursor "$(pwd)"
```

Common operations:

- Inbox: `~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/inbox.sh <team> <agent>`
- Send: `~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/send.sh <team> <from> <to> "<message>"`
- History: `~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/history.sh <team> [agent] [limit]`
- Team: `~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/team.sh <team>`
- Delivery status: `~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/delivery.sh status cursor "$(pwd)"`
- Delivery mode: `~/.agents/skills/__SKILL_NAME__/scripts/delivery.sh set <turn|off> cursor "$(pwd)"`

Cursor delivery supports only `turn` and `off`. Do not use `monitor` or `both`.

`turn` mode is configured in `.cursor/hooks.json` and runs `check-inbox-cursor.sh`
from `hooks.stop[]`. When unread messages exist, the hook returns
`followup_message`. Cursor does not use Codex-style `decision:block` or
`systemMessage`.

If multiple agmsg identities match this same `(project, cursor)` registration,
the turn hook may return `{}`. Resolve the identity first, then check inbox or
send messages with the scripts above.
